  "published": "2026-08-25T04:05:45.59Z",
  "releaseNotes": "TCMProject.Common + TCMProject.Infrastructure (SCH-48): adds a nullable PractitionerUid to IUserLogged/UserLogged, and AuthenticatedUser now reads the \"practitionerUid\" claim from the token. This exposes the authenticated worker's identity to services, so the actor of an action (who approved/rejected an absence, who registered a schedule block) is taken from the token instead of the request body (scheduleeasycore SCH-48). Nullable by design: absent in tokens issued before SCH-48 and for users with no practitioner, which is what enables graceful degradation — falling back to the parameter received from the client during the transition. Non-breaking, additive.",
